            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Mandarin for age-old, then the Mandarin for a script for a language."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: 当年",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "当年 — dāngnián — \"back then; in those years\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "当年他常常给我写信 dāngnián tā chángcháng gěi wǒ xiě xìn — Back then he often sent me letters."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "当年 (dāngnián) is built from 当 'to face, that very' and 年 'a year', both inherited from Middle Chinese, tang and nen (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the first 'to face' and 'to match' and says that when the grain ripens it is called a year."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
